Body:
Based on current codebase, one can configure `clangd` using the following config:

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "lsp": {
    "clangd": {
      "command": ["C:\\msys64\\ucrt64\\bin\\clangd.exe", "--background-index", "--clang-tidy"]
    }
  }
}
```

You can use a project-level `opencode.jsonc` to override the global config if your different projects uses different clangd and/or with different clangd configuration. My own use-case is not embedded development but at least for my own use-case (MSYS2 C++ development) it works as intended.

@ZimaBlueee it's Java env variable - beware "it might be disabled". 

https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/platform/jvmti/jvmti.html#tooloptions

JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS and JAVA_OPTIONS are environment variable that can be used to pass JVM arguments via environment variable instead of CLI arguments.
